- How would you extend to n templates and multilingual prompts?
- How would you test guardrail effectiveness under prompt injections?

## Why This Is Asked

Real-world fintech data assistants service multiple tenants; the router must enforce per-tenant policies, guard against data leakage, and handle conflicting signals and latency constraints.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant-aware policy retrieval and governance
- Guardrails and data-redaction
- Edge-case handling: conflicting signals, missing policy, leakage

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-router sketch
async function routePrompt(prompt, tenantId){
  const policy = await fetchPolicy(tenantId);
  if(!policy) throw new Error('Missing policy');
  if(!policy.allow(prompt)) throw new Error('Action not allowed');

  const intent = analyzeIntent(prompt);
  const module = selectModule(intent, policy);
  const plan = generatePlan(module, intent);

  return { module, plan, payload: buildPayload(module, prompt) };
}
```
